    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3-flash-preview",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "Gemini 3 Flash Preview"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Process: {{ $json.process }}\nDescription: {{ $json.description }}\nFrequency per month: {{ $json.freq_month }}\nMinutes per execution: {{ $json.minutes }}\nPeople involved: {{ $json.people }}\nSystems: {{ $json.systems }}"
            },
            {
              "content": "You are an assistant that triages internal process-automation requests.\nAnalyze the request and return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown).\n\nSCOPE\n- in_scope = true: recurring, rule-based, digital process (data transfer, reporting, notifications, approvals, document processing, syncs between systems).\n- in_scope = false: one-off projects, purchases, hardware/infrastructure incidents, bug reports, strategic or HR-policy decisions, work based on human negotiation or judgment, office/facilities matters.\n- Decide scope FIRST. Missing details never make a request out of scope, and an out-of-scope request never needs clarification.\n\nCRITICAL GAPS (the only reason to mark data as incomplete)\nList in \"critical_gaps\" ONLY items from this closed list that cannot be inferred from the form:\n 1. \"what_is_done\" - the description does not say what is done manually, only a wish (\"automate it\", \"make it faster\").\n 2. \"systems\" - no system or tool involved is named or inferable.\n 3. \"frequency\" - frequency per month is missing or 0.\n 4. \"duration\" - minutes per execution is missing or 0.\nIf the description, systems, frequency and duration are enough to understand the process, critical_gaps MUST be an empty array.\nDo not invent numbers; if frequency or duration is missing, return 0.\n\nNOT critical (never put into critical_gaps)\nAPI availability, file formats, authentication/MFA, storage location, field mapping, matching rules, access rights. These are implementation details for the analysis stage. Put them (max 3) into \"questions_for_author\" as \"nice to know\"; they do not affect the decision.\n\nCONTRADICTIONS\nIf the description and the \"systems\" field clearly contradict each other (a different target system, a different channel), add \"systems\" to critical_gaps and ask one question about it.\n\nOUTPUT JSON\n{\n \"category\": \"reporting|data_sync|notification|approval|workflow|document_processing|other\",\n \"automation_type\": \"integration|RPA|workflow|AI|not_automatable\",\n \"complexity\": \"Low|Medium|High\",\n \"priority\": \"Low|Medium|High\",\n \"in_scope\": true|false,\n \"scope_reason\": \"one sentence\",\n \"summary\": \"one sentence in English\",\n \"critical_gaps\": [],\n \"questions_for_author\": []\n}",
              "role": "model"
            }
          ]
        },
        "jsonOutput": true,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        448,
        0
      ],
      "id": "b6ff8bb1-6ac8-4fbf-82c4-f7834165f92a",
      "name": "AI: parse request",
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Google Gemini(PaLM) Api account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const MIN_ANNUAL_HOURS = 1;\n\nconst f = $('Edit Fields').item.json;\n\nlet raw = $json?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text ?? $json?.text ?? $json?.output ?? '';\nraw = String(raw).replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\nlet g = {};\ntry { g = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { g = {}; }\n\nconst freq = Number(f.freq_month) || 0;\nconst mins = Number(f.minutes) || 0;\nconst desc = String(f.description || '').trim();\nconst sys  = String(f.systems || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n\nconst monthly = Math.round(freq * mins / 60 * 10) / 10;\nconst annual  = Math.round(monthly * 12);\nconst inScope = g.in_scope === true || g.in_scope === 'true';\n\nconst gaps = new Set(Array.isArray(g.critical_gaps) ? g.critical_gaps : []);\nif (inScope) {\n  if (freq <= 0) gaps.add('frequency');\n  if (mins <= 0) gaps.add('duration');\n  if (desc.length < 40) gaps.add('what_is_done');\n  if (!sys || ['-', 'none', 'n/a', 'нет'].includes(sys)) gaps.add('systems');\n}\nconst dataComplete = !inScope || gaps.size === 0;\n\nlet decision;\nif (!inScope) decision = 'Rejected';\nelse if (!dataComplete) decision = 'Needs clarification';\nelse if (annual < MIN_ANNUAL_HOURS) decision = 'Rejected';\nelse decision = 'Accepted';\n\nreturn { json: {\n  ...f,\n  submitted_at: f.submittedAt || new Date().toISOString(),\n  category: g.category, automation_type: g.automation_type,\n  complexity: g.complexity, priority: g.priority,\n  summary: g.summary, scope_reason: g.scope_reason,\n  questions_for_author: JSON.stringify(g.questions_for_author || []),\n  monthly_hours: monthly, annual_hours: annual,\n  in_scope: inScope, data_complete: dataComplete,\n  missing_info: JSON.stringify([...gaps]),\n  decision\n} };"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        784,
        0
      ],
      "id": "3378de75-a27f-4888-8c09-410e3339c6bb",
      "name": "Calculate value"
